
# links
- label: originAppLink gives a Codex session recorded on this machine (no host) Open in Codex to codex://threads/<thread id>, the uuid at the end of its rollout file name, whether or not the session is running
  id: oalcdx
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'Codex' test/browser/origin-app-link.test.js
  tags: [spec, origin-app-links, implemented]
- label: originAppLink gives a Claude Code session recorded on this machine that is not running Open in Claude to claude://resume?session=<session id>, the uuid file name of its transcript under .claude/projects/<project>/ (the link `claude --desktop --resume <id>` opens in Claude Desktop); a running session or a subagent transcript gets none
  id: oalcld
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'Claude Code' test/browser/origin-app-link.test.js
  tags: [spec, origin-app-links, implemented]
- label: originAppLink returns null for any session with a host (imported from another machine), since a native app opens sessions on the machine where they were recorded
  id: oalloc
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'only sessions recorded on this machine' test/browser/origin-app-link.test.js
  tags: [spec, origin-app-links, implemented]
- label: originAppLink returns null for Cursor, Cursor Cloud, Factory, Grok, vktr, fx, DeepSeek Harness and OpenCode sessions, including ones run in a Kandev task folder; none of those apps (nor Kandev) registers a native link to one existing session
  id: oalnone
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'no per-session link' test/browser/origin-app-link.test.js
  tags: [spec, origin-app-links, implemented]

# ui
- label: in hub mode the read-only bar of a running session (#liveTailForm) shows #originAppBar, Open in <App> with the session's originAppLink href (a running local Codex session gets codex://threads/<id>), and no button when the session has no link (a running Grok session in a Kandev task folder)
  id: oalbar
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'read-only bar' test/browser/origin-app-link.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, origin-app-links, implemented]
- label: the Runs side panel header shows #sessionFlyoutOrigin, Open in <App> with the open run's originAppLink href next to Open full page (local Codex, local finished Claude Code), and hides it for an imported Codex session and a Grok session in a Kandev task folder
  id: oalfly
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'Runs side panel' test/browser/origin-app-link.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, origin-app-links, implemented]
